    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured audit event for owner creation.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable Java `record` with components in the spec's order: `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. It:\n   - Serializes to compact JSON via a shared Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) `JsonMapper`, matching the project's existing idiom in `BindingErrorsResponse`.\n   - Carries the event type constant `OWNER_CREATED`.\n   - Exposes a `of(long seq, Owner owner)` factory that reads the owner's **current primary identifier** \u2014 today `owner.getCustomerCode()` \u2014 in one place. When the customer code is later unified into the member id, only this factory changes and the event automatically carries the member id.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a static `AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ` giving a monotonically increasing sequence across creates, and emitted the structured event on the same dedicated `AUDIT` logger right after the existing human-readable audit line:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(OwnerCreatedEvent.of(AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ.incrementAndGet(), owner).toJson());\n   ```\n\nThe event line produced looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n**Design notes:** immutability comes from using a `record` (the value can't be mutated between construction and logging \u2014 the property an audit trail needs); the sequence is process-wide and thread-safe; and the primary-identifier extraction is isolated to the factory so the future customerCode\u2192memberId change is a one-line edit.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` and the full test suite both pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
